Z||000000||BPacholka||10-03-2001||02:55 PM||||I would like to know what 15 inch rims would fit on an 85 GT. I am going junkyard crawling this weekend and would like to know what to look for. If I stay with a 5 on 100 bolt pattern, will any rim work. I have 14 inch wheels right now. Sorry if this is a dumb question, I searched the archive and couldnt find an answer. I found a link to a list of wheels, but the link was bad. If anyone has the list I would appreciate it.<p>[This message has been edited by BPacholka (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Voytek||10-03-2001||06:30 PM||||I believe there is an offset you need to watch for.  If you don't, the tires may end up rubbing the shocks/springs.  Try doing a search on offset - Flashy asked the same question at one point.<P>good luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||10-03-2001||06:46 PM||||Here is a list compiled by Haze before. It is a list of ALL cars that have the 5 X 100mm bolt pattern. Just start looking around and when you find a set measure the offset. If I remember most are very close to the Fiero.<BR>BUICK<BR>SKYHAWK, SKYLARK, 88-UP<P>SOMERSET <P>CADILLAC<BR>CIMARRON 81-88 <P>CHEVY<BR>BERETTA, CORSICA 87-97 <P>GTU, GTZ, Z-26 89-97 <P>CAVALIER 81-UP <P>Z24 89-UP <P>CELEBRITY 82-90 <P>CITATION 80-85 <P>X-11 81-85 <P>MALIBU, CHEVELLE 97-UP <P>CHRYSLER<BR>LEBARON 86-95<P>LASER, GTS 85-88<P>NEW YORKER 86-93<P>SEBRING CONVERTIBLE 96-UP<P>DODGE<BR>ARIES, 400, 600 86-88<P>DAYTONA, TURBO Z 85-93<P>DYNASTY 88-93<P>LANCER 85-89<P>SHADOW 87-94<P>SPIRIT 89-94<P>STRATUS 95-UP<P>LEXUS<BR>ES, 250 90-93<P>OLDSMOBILE<BR>ACHIEVA 92-97<P>CUTLASS CALAIS, 82-89<BR>CIERA, FIRENZA<P>PLYMOUTH<BR>ACCLAIM 89-95<P>BREEZE 95-UP<P>CARAVELLE 85-88<P>LASER 85-89<P>RS, TURBO 85-89<P>NEON 5-LUG 95-99<P>RELIANT, TOURISMO 85-89<P>SUNDANCE 87-94<P>PONTIAC<BR>6000, LE 82-90<P>FIERO, GT 84-88<P>GRANDAM 85-98<BR>SE, GT 85-98<P>SUNBIRD, J2000 82-94<P>SUNFIRE GT 95-UP<P>TOYOTA<BR>CAMRY 86-91<P>CELICA 92-00<P>VOLKSWAGEN<BR>BEETLE 99-UP<P>CORRADO VR6 92-93<P>JETTAIII (4CYL) 99-UP<P>JETTAIII VR6 93-UP<P>GLX VR6 92-98<P>GOLF 2000<P><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gerald||10-03-2001||09:51 PM||||Keep in mind that the rim offset on your car is 35mm. A different offset can change the feel of the car or cause the tire to rub if the diffrence is extream enuf||||reg||1
